{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::version` identifies the version of the review rules and the\ncompleted answer's encoding:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Version of these review rules and the result's encoding.\n    /// Change it when an old answer should no longer be reused.\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`,\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.question_path`, and version identify\nthe same question for checking and execution. Parameters that change which\nquestion is being asked belong in its identity or version.\n\n[Storage](evidence.md#identify-the-saved-assessment) explains how the source node\nand criterion path identify a saved answer and how its version is recorded.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject asks that `Criterion::version` identify the version of the review rules and answer encoding. Together with the source node and criterion path, it identifies the same question, so a changed version means an old answer is no longer reused. One test is marked `{test}` for it: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]`. Its criterion is `Review`, whose `version()` returns `CriterionVersion::new(self.revision)`.\n\n- **Version recorded and compatible with itself:** The test verifies `Review{node 9, \"v1\"}` and stores the evidence. It reloads the answer and asserts `review().version().is_compatible_with(cached.version())`. A false answer is cached and reloaded as `!cached.output().result`.\n- **Different node is a different question:** A `Review` on node 8 with the same \"v1\" version loads as `None`. The source node therefore takes part in the identity.\n- **Changed version means the old answer is not reusable:** Loading with `Review{node 9, \"v2\"}` returns the old record. The test asserts `old.version().unwrap().as_str() == \"v1\"` and `!v2.version().is_compatible_with(old.version())`. It then re-verifies and stores a replacement. It asserts that the stored record's version is now \"v2\", so the new version is recorded with the answer.\n- **Evidence with no recorded version:** The test clears the stored version and asserts that `CriterionVersion::new(\"v2\")` is compatible with the legacy record.\n- **Version comparison rules:** `wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors` tabulates the comparison cases, including prefix, case and `*` handling. It is not marked for this subject, but it adds coverage.\n- **Parameters that change the question belong in identity or version:** This is a design rule, and the test models it by putting `revision` into the version. Other test criteria, such as `ParseAnswer` with \"json-boolean-v1\", also supply versions.\n\nOne point I considered is that the test's `Review` always uses an empty criterion path, so it does not vary the path. Path identity is a separate obligation under `criterion_trait` and the evidence-identity requirements, not under this version requirement. I do not count it as a gap here.\n\nI found no gap in the assertions or the obligations assessed here.",
  "references": "9d1262279cbc6fdf48f62348b85ccec06e728abcb77450a3b226ffc50df6772f",
